# Code owners for Yoda-Man/yodaman
#
# Sole maintainer. One line, because that is the truth.
#
# WHY THIS FILE USED TO DO NOTHING
# --------------------------------
# It previously listed seven per-directory owners using GitHub team syntax
# (@Yoda-Man/core-maintainers, @Yoda-Man/backend-maintainers, ...). Team syntax
# is only valid inside a GitHub *organization*, and Yoda-Man is a personal user
# account — so no such team could exist. GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS
# entries it cannot resolve, which meant the file assigned no reviewer to any
# pull request from the day it was added, while the audit tracker recorded
# "SR-03 Resolved — Added CODEOWNERS".
#
# HONEST LIMITS OF THIS FILE
# --------------------------
# With a single maintainer, CODEOWNERS cannot enforce review: GitHub will not
# request a review from the author of a pull request. This file is therefore
# documentation of ownership, not a control. Treat it as the answer to "who do I
# escalate to", not as a review gate.
#
# If a second maintainer joins, add them here first — that is what turns this
# file from a label into an actual gate.

* @Yoda-Man
